    {
      "id": "c1c539efdb46-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "Points Q, P and R are on a circle with centre O such that &ang;QOR = 116&deg;. If PR is produced to a point M such that &ang;PMQ = 35&deg; , then find the measure of &ang;PQM (in degrees).",
      "questionHtml": "Points Q, P and R are on a circle with centre O such that &ang;QOR = 116&deg;. If PR is produced to a point M such that <span style=\"\">&ang;PMQ = 35&deg;</span>, then find the measure of &ang;PQM (in degrees).",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "135 &deg;",
          "html": "135<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "87 &deg;",
          "html": "87<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "35 &deg;",
          "html": "35<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "58 &deg;",
          "html": "58<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Given:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&ang;PMQ = 35&deg; and&nbsp;&ang;QOR = 116&deg;&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Concept used:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">The sum of all interior angles of a triangle is 180&deg;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">In the case of the circum-center, the angle at the center is twice the angle at the circumference.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Calculation:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/04/F1_Shraddha_SSC_06.04.2022_D4.png\" style=\"width: 287px; height: 197px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">O being the circum-center,&nbsp;<span style=\"\">&ang;QPR = 116&nbsp;&divide; 2= 58&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">Considering&nbsp;&Delta;QPM,</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&ang;PQM +&nbsp;&ang;QPM +&nbsp;&ang;PMQ = 180&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;PQM = (180 - 58 - 35)&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;&ang;PQM = 87</span><span style=\"\">&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong><span style=\"\">&there4; The measure of the&nbsp;&ang;PQM is&nbsp;87</span><span style=\"\">&deg;.</span></strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/04/F1_Shraddha_SSC_06.04.2022_D4.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c1c539efdb46-q5",
      "number": 5,
      "question": "Two circles have radii of 27 cm and 36 cm. The distance between their centres is 45 cm. What is the length (in cm) of their common chord?",
      "questionHtml": "Two circles have radii of 27 cm and 36 cm. The distance between their centres is 45 cm. What is the length (in cm) of their common chord?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "47.5 cm",
          "html": "47.5 cm&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "40.5 cm",
          "html": "40.5 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "37.2 cm",
          "html": "37.2 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "43.2 cm",
          "html": "43.2 cm"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>√((4 × 27<sup>2</sup> × 45<sup>2</sup> - (27<sup>2</sup> - 36<sup>2</sup> + 45<sup>2</sup>)<sup>2</sup>) / (4 × 45<sup>2</sup>)),</p>\n\n<p>√((4 × 729 × 2025 - (729 - 1296 + 2025)<sup>2</sup>) / (4 × 2025)),</p>\n\n<p>√((5904900 - 1458<sup>2</sup>) / 8100) ⇒ √(3779136 / 8100) <span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">⇒</span>√(466.56), 43.2 cm</p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
