      "id": "c1c539efdb46-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "If two circles of radii 28 cm and 18 cm touch each other externally, then the length of a common tangent is _________. [Give your answer correct to 2 decimal places.]",
      "questionHtml": "If two circles of radii 28 cm and 18 cm touch each other externally, then the length of a common tangent is _________. [Give your answer correct to 2 decimal places.]",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "40.90 cm",
          "html": "40.90 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "42.00 cm",
          "html": "42.00 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "44.90 cm",
          "html": "44.90 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "44.12 cm",
          "html": "44.12 cm"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/12/F2_Vinanti_SSC_19.12.22_D1.png\" style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41); height: 125px; width: 189px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Length of common tangent = 2√(28 cm × 18 cm) = 2√(504 cm<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>) = 2 × √(504 cm<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>) ≈ 2 × 22.47 cm ≈ 44.90 cm (rounded to 2 decimal places)</p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/12/F2_Vinanti_SSC_19.12.22_D1.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c1c539efdb46-q8",
      "number": 8,
      "question": "In the given figure, a smaller circle touches a larger circle at P and passes through its centre O. PR is a chord of the larger circle and PS is a chord of the smaller circle of length 15 cm and RQ is 16 cm, then what is the length (in cm) of the radius of the larger circle?",
      "questionHtml": "<p>In the given figure, a smaller circle touches a larger circle at P and passes through its centre O. PR is a chord of the larger circle and PS is a chord of the smaller circle of length 15 cm and RQ is 16 cm, then what is the length (in cm) of the radius of the larger circle?</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/11/F3_Savita_SSC_28-11-22_D2.png\" style=\"width: 182px; height: 224px;\" /></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "10",
          "html": "10"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "17",
          "html": "17"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "22",
          "html": "22"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "4",
          "html": "4"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n\n<p>PS = 15 cm</p>\n\n<p>RQ = 16 cm</p>\n\n<p><strong>Concept used:</strong></p>\n\n<p>If the three sides of one triangle are proportional to the three sides of another, then the two triangles are similar.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/11/F3_Savita_SSC_28-11-22_D3.png\" style=\"width: 207px; height: 250px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>In the given figure,</p>\n\n<p>&ang;RPQ =&nbsp;&ang;SPO [Common angle]</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&ang;PRQ =&nbsp;&ang;PSO [Angles of the semi circle]</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">So,</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&Delta;PRQ&nbsp;&sim;&nbsp;&Delta;PSO</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">PR/PS&nbsp;= PQ/PO</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">PR/15 = 2/1&nbsp; &nbsp; [PQ diameter of the larger circle]</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; PR = 30</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">Now,</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">PQ<sup>2</sup></span>&nbsp;= 30<sup>2</sup> + 16<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span style=\"\">PQ<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;= 900</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;+ 256</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">PQ<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;= 1156</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;PQ<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&nbsp;= 34<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;PQ</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;= 34</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">So, radius = 34/2 = 17 cm</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong><span style=\"\">&there4;&nbsp;The length (in cm) of the radius of the larger circle is 17.</span></strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/11/F3_Savita_SSC_28-11-22_D2.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/11/F3_Savita_SSC_28-11-22_D3.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
